.Dd $Mdocdate: August 2 2026 $
.Dt Fugu::MQTT 3p
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm Fugu::MQTT
.Nd a subscribing MQTT client for a single-threaded daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Bd -literal
use Fugu::MQTT;

my $mqtt = Fugu::MQTT->new(
    host => '127.0.0.1',
    port => 1883,
);
$mqtt->mqtt_connect(10) or die "no broker\en";

$mqtt->subscribe('stat/+/RESULT', sub ($topic, $payload) {
    ...
});
$mqtt->publish('cmnd/lamp/POWER', 'ON');

# From the event loop, once each pass
$mqtt->tick;
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a wrapper around
.Xr Net::MQTT::Simple 3p
for a daemon that has one process and one event loop.
It never blocks the caller.
.Fn tick
drains what arrived and returns, thus the loop keeps the MQTT
connection beside its own descriptors.
.Pp
.Xr Net::MQTT::Simple 3p
loads at connect time, not at compile time.
Thus the module keeps the core-Perl load contract of Fugu, and a
daemon whose broker is optional still starts without the library.
.Pp
Every message goes through a callback.
The module holds the incoming messages in a queue and dispatches them
in
.Fn tick ,
in the process that called it.
A callback thus runs where the caller can reason about it, and never
inside a signal handler.
.Ss new
.Fn new "%args"
creates a client.
The method opens no socket.
Call
.Fn mqtt_connect .
.Pp
These are the arguments:
.Bl -tag -width "usernameXX"
.It Fa host
The broker.
The default is 127.0.0.1.
.It Fa port
The broker port.
The default is 1883.
.It Fa username
The login name.
The client sends no credentials when this argument is absent.
.It Fa password
The login password.
.El
.Ss mqtt_connect
.Fn mqtt_connect "$timeout"
connects to the broker.
The default timeout is 10 seconds.
.Pp
A connect can block in the resolver or in the handshake, and no poll
loop can interrupt either.
Thus the guard is the alarm of
.Xr Fugu::Timeout 3p .
A broker that does not answer costs the caller the timeout, not the
run.
.Pp
The method returns true when the client is connected.
.Ss subscribe
.Fn subscribe "$topic" "$callback"
registers a topic and its callback.
The callback gets
.Fa ( $topic , $payload ) ,
where the topic is the one that arrived, not the pattern.
.Pp
The pattern accepts the MQTT wildcards:
.Sq +
matches one level and
.Sq #
matches the remaining levels.
The module registers the subscription even when the client is not
connected, so a caller can subscribe before the broker is up.
.Fn resubscribe
sends the set again after a reconnection.
.Ss publish
.Fn publish "$topic" "$payload" "$retain"
sends one message.
A true
.Fa $retain
makes the broker keep the message for the next subscriber.
The method does nothing when the client is not connected.
.Ss tick
.Fn tick "$timeout"
reads what arrived and runs the callbacks.
The default timeout is 0, which does not block.
The method returns the number of dispatched messages.
.Pp
The method reports a lost connection: it clears the connected state
and returns 0.
The caller then calls
.Fn reconnect
on a schedule of its own.
.Ss reconnect
.Fn reconnect
disconnects, connects again, and subscribes again.
The method returns 1 on success and 0 on failure.
.Ss resubscribe
.Fn resubscribe
sends every registered subscription to the broker again.
.Fn reconnect
calls it.
A caller needs it only when it connects by itself.
.Ss disconnect
.Fn disconnect
closes the connection and discards the queued messages.
The registered subscriptions stay, thus a later
.Fn reconnect
restores them.
.Ss is_connected
.Fn is_connected
reports if the client holds a connection.
.Ss subscriptions
.Fn subscriptions
returns the registered topic patterns.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn mqtt_connect
and
.Fn is_connected
return true when the client is connected.
.Fn reconnect
returns 1 or 0.
.Fn tick
returns a count.
.Fn subscriptions
returns a list.
.Pp
No method dies.
A broker error, a bad callback, and a lost connection all go to the
log of
.Xr Fugu::Log 3p .
A daemon must not exit because a broker went away.
.Sh EXAMPLES
This example reconnects when the broker goes away:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$loop->every(1, sub {
	$mqtt->tick;
	$mqtt->reconnect unless $mqtt->is_connected;
});
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr Fugu::Log 3p ,
.Xr Fugu::Timeout 3p ,
.Xr Net::MQTT::Simple 3p
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Dick Olsson Aq Mt hi@senzilla.io
.Sh CAVEATS
A callback runs inside
.Fn tick .
A callback that blocks blocks the loop.
Keep the work in a callback short, or queue it.
.Pp
The module holds no quality of service beyond what
.Xr Net::MQTT::Simple 3p
gives, which is QoS 0.
A message can be lost.
A caller that must know a device answered reads the state topic of
that device.
